<p class="eyebrow">How the number gets built</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom:22px">Four things set your fare — nothing else.</h2>
<ul class="points">
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Route.</b> Distance between your pickup and drop-off. Airport, port and city routes are published above; anything else is quoted individually before you book.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Time of day.</b> A 30% supplement applies between midnight and 6 a.m. — it's built into the quoted fare, never added after the ride.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>Wait time beyond the complimentary window.</b> 60 minutes are included at airports and FBOs; time held beyond that is the only variable added after booking, and it's agreed with you in advance, not discovered afterward.</span></li>
<li><i class="mark"></i><span><b>The calendar.</b> A handful of dates a year — Art Basel, major boat shows, F1, Ultra — put real pressure on vehicle availability across every operator in South Florida, ours included. Those dates are quoted individually, always before you confirm.</span></li>
</ul>
<p style="color:var(--muted);margin-top:22px;max-width:640px">That's the entire list. No membership tiers, no surge multiplier, no "premium demand" language — just the four inputs above, quoted in writing before you decide.</p>
</div>
