<p class="eyebrow">Policy, in detail</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom:22px">Reservation, cancellation, wait time, and disruptions.</h2>
<div class="wrap faq reveal" style="padding:0">
<details><summary>How does a reservation get confirmed?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">You receive a fixed quote in writing before anything is booked. The reservation is confirmed once you accept that quote — vehicle and chauffeur are then held specifically for your date and time.</div></details>
<details><summary>How much complimentary wait time do I get?<span class="pm">+</span></summary><div class="ans">60 minutes at airports and FBOs, measured from actual landing, not the scheduled time. 15 minutes on hotel, residence, and other pickups.</div></details>
<details><summary>What is your cancellation policy?</summary><div class="ans">Free cancellation up to 2 hours before pickup. A no-show, or a cancellation inside that window without a qualifying reason (flight cancellation, medical emergency), may require prepayment or a card on file before any future booking is confirmed.</div></details>
<details><summary>What if my flight is delayed or cancelled?</summary><div class="ans">A delayed flight is tracked automatically and never charged extra for the wait within the complimentary window. A cancelled flight carries no charge at all — let us know as soon as you know.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is there a supplement for late-night pickups?</summary><div class="ans">Yes — a 30% supplement applies to pickups between midnight and 6 a.m. It's included in the fare you're quoted, not added afterward.</div></details>
<details><summary>Are your rates per person or per vehicle?</summary><div class="ans">Per vehicle. The fare is the same whether one passenger rides or the Suburban is full.</div></details>
<details><summary>Where do you operate?</summary><div class="ans">Miami-Dade, Broward, and Palm Beach counties. See the <a href="service-area.html">service area</a> page for specific neighborhoods and drive-time context.</div></details>
</div>
</div>
</section>

